<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malta is an island country in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, made up of Malta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gozo">Gozo</a> and smaller islands. Its harbours drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, who took it in 870, and Normans; from 1530 it was the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>, who withstood the Ottoman Great Siege of 1565 and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valletta">Valletta</a>. A British colony from 1800, it became independent in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malta.jpg" alt="Malta" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From 835 Aghlabid forces campaigned in Calabria and Apulia, taking Amantea, Taranto and Bari, but the destruction of a Muslim fleet off Ostia in 849 halted the advance, and <b>Malta</b> was conquered in 870.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aghlabid-emirate">Aghlabid emirate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…of Lauria won a series of victories against the Angevins after Peter III took Sicily in 1282: off <b>Malta</b> in 1283, in the Bay of Naples in 1284, where Charles of Salerno was captured, and at Les Formigues in 1285, which wrecked the French invasion known as the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>European settlers came from France, Spain, Italy and <b>Malta</b>; a law of 1889 made the children of foreign Europeans born in Algeria French, and by 1954 there were about a million Europeans, later called pieds-noirs, beside some eight to nine million Muslim Algerians.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1530 the Knights Hospitaller held <b>Malta</b> as a fief of the kingdom, paying the king of Sicily an annual tribute of a single falcon.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sicily">Kingdom of Sicily · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Gaiseric conquered Sicily, Sardinia, Corsica, <b>Malta</b> and the Balearic Islands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/vandal-kingdom">Vandal Kingdom · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>From the 9th century BCE Phoenicians founded Carthage and other Punic communities in North Africa, southern Spain, Sardinia, western Sicily and <b>Malta</b>, where Punic religion continued the Phoenician branch with local differences.</blockquote><a href="/religion/canaanite-religion">Canaanite religion · Spread</a></li></ul></section>
